WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.560
Imagine a world where we get what we all
deserve: A good death.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.820
Nothing seems much different. The world is much the same as it is now.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.780
People do the same sorts of things,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.360
have much the same joys and pains. They're born, they grow up, they work, they play,

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.700
have families, love argue, enjoy
their brief time on Earth.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.320
And die.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.519
It's just that if you go to the outskirts of
any town there's a new facility there.

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:33.989
It looks like a Medical Center. It is, in a
way. A well-designed building with nice

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:38.720
landscaping and a free car park. If you
go inside you'll discover what's going on.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.300
The receptionist can explain.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.120
There are leaflets too. Everything is well ordered
and calm.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.920
Doctors, psychologists, counsellors and nurses work here.  But so too do specialists lawyers.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.400
This is the "Good Death Centre", provided on the National Health Service.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.460
Those who don't want to descend into the indignity of extreme dementia, or doubt the ability of

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.480
palliative care to ease their exit from
life, will come here when the time is right.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:10.460
They'll choose the moments of
their own deaths. Most of us have a death

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.700
plan and a living will now. It's a great
comfort to know that the option exists

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.380
if the going gets too tough.  We've heard
euthanasia for pets for a very long time

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.040
but before the good death centres we
forced our friends and relatives to

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.980
endure months and sometimes years of
agony and indignity against their will.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:33.520
For what? They now seems so cruel, so
unnecessary, so pointless.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:37.880
Of course there are safeguards. No one
gets to use the facility without

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:42.770
thorough psychological examination and
counselling. This choice is only for the

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:47.210
sound of mind and those who have
demonstrated a genuine desire to die by

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:51.890
these means. You need a good reason such
as a painful terminal illness

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:56.290
or the first signs of dementia. Consent has to be informed. Life is much better now.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:00.560
It's reassuring to know you don't have
to endure it even when you've lost the

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.720
power to take your own life. 
I have my own death plan.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:09.880
If I don't die my sleep, I expect to die in a Good Death Centre.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:14.620
It's a comforting thought. You should think about it.

